GHC 6.2.2 -- mhs: Functor/Applicative/MonadFail instances
Modern base makes Applicative a superclass of Monad and moves fail to
MonadFail; MicroHs implements the modern hierarchy. Every monad the
compiler defines with `instance Monad` (CgMonad FCode, DsMonad DsM,
TcRnTypes TcRn, FlattenMonad Flatten, JavaGen LifterM, ByteCodeItbls
State, the ilxGen test IIO) gets the two superclass instances, and its
`fail` moves to MonadFail. In ByteCodeItbls the tuple pattern under >>=
is taken apart with case, because mhs asks for MonadFail for a refutable
lambda pattern. Same as 4.08.2's patch 0012.

